      <p>The original Ready or Not (2019) was a tight, clever horror-comedy that said what it had to say in 97 minutes and left. The sequel returns to the class-warfare and feminist messaging of the first film without the precision that made those themes land. Where the original wore its ideology efficiently, this one uses it as the primary engine rather than a backdrop. The result is a film that is ideologically louder than it is effective, leaning into its progressive framing as though audience familiarity with the first film has earned it more latitude than the storytelling supports. A -13 WOKE margin confirms the sequel amplified rather than restrained the original's ideological content.</p>
