  <p>Twenty-five years after the original, the franchise delivers what fans consider its best installment. Bloodlines adds a generational element with a family that has been outrunning death for decades. The scores are both low, reflecting a film designed to entertain with elaborate kill sequences rather than make arguments. The slight traditional edge reflects a story that treats mortality seriously without exploiting it ideologically.</p>
