  <p>Replace the dog from Cujo with a chimpanzee, move the setting to a gorgeous Hawaiian cliff house, and crank the gore to eleven. Primate is a contained creature feature that earns its horror elements through practical threat rather than ideology. The modest traditional edge reflects a film that centers family protection and parental sacrifice without embedding progressive messaging in the horror framework.</p>
